00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.790
Despite all the attention
lately, machine learning still

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.080
remains somewhat difficult to
build, maintain, and deploy.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.450
Thankfully for you,
Google Cloud Platform

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.550
puts a lot of that
behind the scenes,

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.190
so you don't have
to worry about it.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.850
So what does the
[? hello ?] world of ML

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.870
look like when you don't have to
write the neural nets yourself?

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.090
Simply calling the
Vision API to describe

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.980
what it finds in the picture.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.620
As a leader in machine
learning, Google Cloud

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.610
offers several high-quality
pre-trained models via APIs

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.610
that can easily be consumed
by developers regardless

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.150
of the language they use or the
nature of their application.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.150
Developers can invoke
the API directly or using

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.100
one of the idiomatic
client libraries

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.500
available in numerous
programming languages.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.830
Here, we invoke the API directly
from the product description

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:02.670
page.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.940
From this image, the API can
detect a broad set of labels,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.730
provide dominant colors,
and other image properties.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.890
It can also extract
text, identify entities,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.630
such as landmarks, celebrities,
logos, or news events

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.960
along millions of
entities that it supports.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.730
It can also moderate content
such as all of your app's

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.740
user-generated content.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.960
In addition to the
Vision API, GCP

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.330
offers pre-trained
models for text

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.200
to speech, speech to text,
natural language, translate,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.240
all via easy-to-use APIs.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.210
Now, pre-trained models
are amazingly easy to use,

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:40.260
as we've seen, but they're not
trained on your setup data.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.720
This is where a Cloud
AutoML comes in.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.440
Cloud AutoML is here to enable
developers with limited machine

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.130
learning expertise to train
high-quality models specific

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.170
to their business
needs by leveraging

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.350
Google's state-of-the-art
transfer learning and neural

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.640
architecture search technology.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.090
Cloud AutoML provides a simple
graphical user interface

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:04.930
for you to train, evaluate,
improve, and deploy models

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.940
based on your own data.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.400
You're only a few minutes
away from your own custom

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.870
machine-learning model.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.600
Now, the ML APIs
and Cloud AutoML

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.700
are great when you
want to use or build

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.820
upon a pre-trained model that
Google already has training

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:19.510
for.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.390
But what if your
needs are beyond that?

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.690
Well, that basically requires
training your own models

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.540
with your own data sets on
your own virtual machines.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.780
And I don't know about
you, but I don't always

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.890
have time for that, which is
why I use Cloud Deep Learning VM

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:36.940
Image.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.070
These Google Compute
Engine instances

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.340
come pre-installed with the
latest versions of TensorFlow,

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.110
PyTorch, and scikit-learn.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.570
You can also add
cloud CPU and GPU

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.550
support with a single click.

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.550
This image also comes with
the latest software drivers

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.330
and third-party dependencies,
including the latest GPU

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.070
software, and is
available using the GCP

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.670
Marketplace from the console
or using the command line.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.490
If you'd like to get the
operations out of the way

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.740
and focus on your
models, consider

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:10.960
using Cloud ML Engine which
offers fully managed training

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.210
and prediction services for
developers and data scientists.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.420
You can build your models
with multiple ML frameworks

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.020
including scikit-learn,
XGBoost, Keras, and, of course,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.430
TensorFlow.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.480
Cloud ML Engine trains
any model at large scale

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.920
on a managed cluster.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.500
HyperTune is a
unique feature that

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.440
enables you to reach
better results faster

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.090
by automatically tuning
deep-learning hyperparameters.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.720
Cloud ML Engine then offers
online predictions, adjusting

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.620
to any requests rate coming from
your ML-enabled applications

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.010
and does so through a
secure web endpoint.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.140
Batch predictions
are also supported

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.450
for really
cost-effective inference

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.250
for asynchronous apps.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.650
Whether you're new
to machine learning

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.530
or you're already an
expert, GCP has a variety

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.990
of tools to help you,
from pre-trained ML

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.140
models accessible
via simple API call,

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.450
to customizing
models with AutoML,

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.140
to training and serving a custom
TensorFlow model using Compute

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.470
Engine or Cloud ML Engine.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.290
Consider taking free codelabs,
linked in the description

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:22.190
below, to explore
these products.

